# 000-KRN-0101 — A launch session holds every launch slot — done

**Type:** `loader` · **Owner:** kernel session · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-10-20) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** — · **Constitution:** MC-3.11, MC-3.3

## Problem

The tools track (requests-KRN.md, 2026-10-10, for [211-APP-0044](../issues-done/211-APP-0044-console-joined-to-the-shell.done)): `loader`'s launch session kept at most 5 grants (`Session.grants: [(u8, usize); 5]`), and a sixth `grant` was refused with `limit`, while `LAUNCH_SLOTS` names 17 slots a launcher may fill.

- `console` started by `wm` may need six: the window, the user's files, system information, the camera, the shell's commands and, for `record -w`, the window to see. The `wm` suite's `record -w` lost its window lease to the limit.
- The tools track grants `SLOT_SHELL` last and lets a start go on without it, so the program runs without the shell's commands when the session is full. On the MacBook Pro `wm` itself now asks for six (211-APP-0070, on the tools branch), the battery last.

## Plan

- **The session holds** a grant for every launch slot and `SLOT_FIRMWARE` (`grant-firmware`): 18. With the loader's five standard clients and the debug mode's log, a spawn carries at most 24 of `SPAWN_GRANTS_MAX` (32), which a compile-time check holds.
- **A grant beyond it** still answers `limit`; a grant in a slot already lent replaces it, as before.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] **The `bench` suite's `check`, on x86 and aarch64:** a launcher lends an endpoint in each of the 17 launch slots in one session, and the program says it holds every one (`launch: every slot`).
- [ ] **The tools track** may then grant `SLOT_SHELL` (and the battery) in the order it likes; its own suites show `console` from `wm` with the shell's commands beside `record -w`'s window lease ([requests-APP.md](../issues/requests-APP.md) gets a note).

## Resolution

In `main` at 289e84b. The gate of 10d3ec3 (`main` 1753bf4 merged), 2026-10-20, passed every group: the host groups and the timing-sensitive x86 groups on un-rizen-service, the other x86 groups on i9, aarch64 half on i9 and half on un-rizen-service. Two x86 groups timed out while other tracks' gates loaded both machines (load average 27 and 32 on 16 threads) and passed when run again on the same tree.

- `launch: every slot` passed in x86: "keys, shell, tools" (`bench` suite, un-rizen-service); aarch64: "programs, shell and four CPUs" (`bench` suite, i9): every `check` row named here passes, as `check_tool_check` requires. ABI 10 has 19 launch slots, not the 17 this issue was written with; the check lends one in each.
- **Left to the tools track:** granting `SLOT_SHELL` and the battery in its own order, and `wm`'s console beside `record -w` (the note in [requests-APP.md](../issues/requests-APP.md)).

